{{!--
    reference/disclosure - inline collapsible section used throughout the API reference:
    example payloads, nested property groups, and the try-it panel. Block form; the block
    is the body:
      {{#> reference/disclosure label="Example response"}} ...body... {{/reference/disclosure}}

    Params:
      label       - summary text (required)
      preview     - muted continuation of the summary, e.g. the first child names of a
                    collapsed property group (optional). "6 properties" on its own gives a
                    reader nothing to decide on, and one tag page renders 135 closed groups
      elId        - element id on the <details> (optional). Deliberately NOT named `id`:
                    Handlebars merges a partial's hash params into the caller's context,
                    so a partial that reads `id` also picks up an `id` that merely
                    happens to be on the surrounding context - and every call site here
                    sits inside an operation whose model has one. That silently emitted
                    the operation id on four elements per operation.
      open        - true to render expanded (optional)
      primary     - true for the larger primary-colored summary (the try-it panel);
                    default is the muted text-xs look used by the example blocks
      class       - extra classes on the <details> (optional; the caller owns spacing)

    The chevron rotation is driven by .ee-ref-disclosure in app.tailwind.css rather than
    Tailwind's group-open variant: these disclosures nest (a property group inside a
    property group), and a named group matches ANY open ancestor, so an inner collapsed
    group's chevron would rotate whenever an outer one was open. The stylesheet uses a
    child combinator, which is exact at every depth.

    Not ui/details: that one hardcodes a card shell plus font-bold text-primary on the
    summary, which is the wrong weight for an inline disclosure inside a card body.
--}}
<details class="ee-ref-disclosure{{#if class}} {{class}}{{/if}}" {{#if elId}}id="{{elId}}" {{/if}}{{#if open}}open{{/if}}>
    <summary
        class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center gap-1 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden {{#if primary}}text-primary hover:text-primary/80 text-sm font-semibold{{else}}text-base-content/60 hover:text-base-content text-xs{{/if}}">
        <span class="ee-ref-chevron icon-[tabler--chevron-right] shrink-0 {{#if primary}}size-4{{else}}size-3.5{{/if}}"></span>
        {{!-- truncate, not just nowrap: the preview is a hint about what is inside the group,
              so it gives up its tail rather than pushing the summary past the viewport --}}
        <span class="min-w-0 truncate">{{label}}{{#if preview}}<span
                class="text-base-content/45 ms-1.5 font-normal">{{preview}}</span>{{/if}}</span>
    </summary>
    {{!-- own hash params are neutralized so they cannot fall through into nested ui/* calls inside the block --}}
    {{> @partial-block label="" preview="" elId="" open="" primary="" class=""}}
</details>
